From d9295eb856552a499db99a9b7b12415fd94102b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 22:01:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] arm64: dts: qcom: x1-microsoft-denali: add a marked D26
 speaker fragment

Add an include-only fragment for a speaker-enabled test variant. It
pulls in the full sound card and the WSA bus and adds the property
/chosen/sp11,speaker-policy, which the project DTB safety check requires
before it accepts an enabled speaker path. The property is a tooling
marker only and no driver reads it.

Nothing includes the file and no packaged DTB changes.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5
---
 .../qcom/x1-microsoft-denali-audio-d26.dtsi   | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali-audio-d26.dtsi

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali-audio-d26.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali-audio-d26.dtsi
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..6a7b4988d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali-audio-d26.dtsi
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
+/*
+ * Surface Pro 11: opt-in speaker variant under project decision D26.
+ *
+ * Enables the full sound card and the WSA8845 SoundWire bus, as in
+ * x1-microsoft-denali-audio-speakers.dtsi, and marks the DTB with
+ * /chosen/sp11,speaker-policy. The project image tooling (kernel-dtb-safety)
+ * accepts an enabled speaker path only in a DTB that carries this marker.
+ *
+ * The marker is a tooling contract. No driver reads it, it is not evidence
+ * of speaker protection and it does not make playback audible: the machine
+ * driver refuses WSA playback until the closed-loop protection is validated.
+ * The packaged default DTB never includes this file.
+ */
+#include "x1-microsoft-denali-audio-speakers.dtsi"
+
+&{/chosen} {
+	sp11,speaker-policy = "d26-open-loop-v1";
+};
